===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[formulate]] a [[theory]], especially about some [[specific]] [[subject]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002| author=Dave Hill | title=Marxism Against Postmodernism in Educational Theory |page=257| passage=Derridean "messianicity ''without'' messianism" that marks so much of post-modernist educational '''theorizing''' today, and that makes use of esotericism, sigetics, acroamatics, proleptics, and illocutionary and perlocutionary acts in the disguise of a new pedagogy of the unknowable, wasn't the answer ten years ago.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2018|author=Bernard Stiegler|title=Automatic Society: The Future of Work|page=152
|passage=There are processes of collective individuation that produce the transindividual in the course of a process of transindividuation (which Simondon does not '''theorize''' as such).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Ryan Lee Cartwright|title=Peculiar Places: A Queer Crip History of White Rural Nonconformity|publisher=University of Chicago Press|isbn=9780226697079|page=188
|passage=Autistic rhetoric scholar Melanie Yergeau '''theorizes''' neuroqueer as a kind of “asocially perverse” motioning.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Selim Algar|title=Incensed owner of $8M Florida mansion ransacked by teens wants them prosecuted|work=w:New York Post|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220703155239/https://nypost.com/2022/06/22/florida-woman-wants-to-prosecute-teens-who-ransacked-mansion-in-wild-party/|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:News Corp|date=22-06-2022|issn=1090-3321|oclc=1097129885|passage=The homeowner '''theorized''' that the intruders saw that the house was up for sale and targeted it for their rager.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[speculate]].

